# The artifact store. Binaries live in the registry, never in git --
# and the pattern is a whole-directory one on purpose. It used to list
# suffixes (*.tar.gz), which silently stopped covering the store the
# day a second artifact kind appeared: the first ISOs published were
# staged for commit by an ordinary `git add -A`. An allow-nothing rule
# cannot fall behind the store's contents that way.
# that separation is the security model, not a size decision: recipes
# are reviewable text in the Cix repository, artifacts are opaque bytes
# here, and the recipe's checksum is what approves them.
cache/blobs/
cache/tmp/
cache/packages/*
cache/*.tar.gz
cache/*.iso

# Build output
build/

# libFuzzer writes a reproducer here when a harness finds something.
# It is not a corpus entry: a real finding gets a named seed under
# fuzz/corpus/ AND a case in the C test suite, because a regression
# that only clang can catch is one `make test` misses everywhere.
crash-*
leak-*
timeout-*
oom-*

# System files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
